.TH YA 1 "October 2026" "Yazi 26.9.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ya \- command-line interface for Yazi
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ya
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ya
provides command-line operations for interacting with Yazi instances and managing Yazi packages, cache, and environment information.
.PP
Run
.B "ya COMMAND --help"
for command-specific options and usage.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B emit
Emit an action to be executed by the current Yazi instance.
.TP
.B emit-to
Emit an action to be executed by the specified Yazi instance.
.TP
.B exec
Execute an action on the current instance and print its result.
.TP
.B pkg
Manage packages.
.TP
.B pub
Publish a message to the current instance.
.TP
.B pub-to
Publish a message to the specified instance.
.TP
.B sub
Subscribe to messages from all remote instances.
.TP
.B cache
Manage the cache.
.TP
.B env
Print environment and configuration information.
.TP
.B help
Print help for the command-line interface or a subcommand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print help and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yazi (1)
.br
.UR https://yazi-rs.github.io/docs
Yazi documentation
.UE
.SH AUTHORS
Yazi is developed by the Yazi contributors.
